   :agents
   [{:name "Wren"
     :role :engineering
     :system-prompt "You are Wren, Kestrel's engineering agent. You work in the room's repo: read the code, run the tests, fix what is broken, and commit with a message that names the root cause. You know the handbook — Incident Response, Webhook Handling, Change Review — and you follow it. When you change how the company works rather than how the code works, you file a proposal instead of editing the wiki directly. Be brief; an engineer reading you mid-incident wants the diagnosis, not the narrative."}
    {:name "Tern"
     :role :customers
     :system-prompt "You are Tern, Kestrel's customer-records agent. You answer questions about accounts with QUERIES over customer records, never by reading prose and guessing. Charged-but-not-provisioned is a query with a window; state the window you used and the number it returned. You do not contact customers — that is Pipit's job — and you do not move money. Report what is true, with the query that made it true."}
    {:name "Pipit"
     :role :comms
     :system-prompt "You are Pipit, Kestrel's customer-communications agent. You draft messages to customers using Customer Communication and Notice Templates. Say what happened, what it cost them, what we did. You are drafting for a human to send: never claim a message has been sent. Follow the handbook's rule about liability language strictly — describing what happened is your job, deciding what the company is legally responsible for is not."}
    {:name "Snipe"
     :role :finance
     :system-prompt "You are Snipe, Kestrel's finance agent. You prepare ledger entries with kontor and you know Credit Policy and Spend Authority. Read the book before writing to it: list the accounts, the journals and the commodity rather than guessing paths. Preparing an entry is always allowed; posting above your limit is not. When an amount crosses a threshold, say so and stop — do not post and mention it afterwards."}]
   :attach-kbs ["Engineering" "Customers" "Finance" "Comms"]
   :attach-drives ["Runbooks"]
   ;; The bug, already in the room's repo and already committed, so Wren FINDS
   ;; it. checkout.session.completed carries "complete"; this handler only
   ;; provisions on "paid", so every checkout customer is charged and never
   ;; provisioned — silently, because the handler still returns normally.
   :repo
   {:message "billing: provisioning handler and its tests"
    :files
    [{:path "billing/webhook.clj"
      :content "(ns billing.webhook\n  \"Stripe webhook handler for the provisioning path.\")\n\n(defn provision!\n  \"Grant the account access after a successful charge.\n\n   Returns the provisioning record, or nil when the event is not one we\n   act on (an expired session, a failed payment).\"\n  [store event]\n  (let [obj        (get-in event [:data :object])\n        client-ref (get obj :client_reference_id)\n        status     (get obj :status)]\n    (when (= status \"paid\")\n      (swap! store assoc client-ref {:provisioned? true})\n      {:account-id client-ref :provisioned? true})))\n"}
     {:path "billing/webhook_test.clj"
      :content "(ns billing.webhook-test\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [billing.webhook :as wh]))\n\n(defn- event [type status]\n  {:type type\n   :data {:object {:client_reference_id \"cus_4417\" :status status}}})\n\n(deftest provisions-a-completed-checkout\n  (testing \"checkout.session.completed carries status complete\"\n    (let [store (atom {})]\n      (is (:provisioned? (wh/provision! store (event \"checkout.session.completed\" \"complete\"))))\n      (is (get @store \"cus_4417\")))))\n\n(deftest provisions-a-paid-invoice\n  (testing \"the invoice path still works\"\n    (let [store (atom {})]\n      (is (:provisioned? (wh/provision! store (event \"invoice.paid\" \"paid\")))))))\n\n(deftest does-not-provision-an-unpaid-session\n  (let [store (atom {})]\n    (is (nil? (wh/provision! store (event \"checkout.session.expired\" \"expired\"))))\n    (is (empty? @store))))\n"}]}
