     :text "Provisioning looked slow over the weekend — two customers emailed asking where their login was. Both resolved themselves within the hour. Worth a look if anyone has time."}
    {:from :agent :at "2026-07-21T15:31:00Z"
     :text "<p>Checked the last 72 hours: 214 checkout sessions, 214 provisioning writes. Ratio is 1.0, so nothing was dropped — the two slow ones were both retries after a Stripe timeout, provisioned on the second attempt 40 and 55 seconds later.</p><p>The alerting in <em>stripe/2026-07-alerts.md</em> only fires below 0.95, so a slow-but-eventually-correct path is invisible to it. That is probably the right threshold; flagging it so we know the gap exists.</p>"}
    {:from :me :at "2026-07-21T15:44:00Z"
     :text "Good, leave the threshold. Slow is survivable, silent isn't."}
    {:from :me :at "2026-07-24T23:02:00Z"
     :text "Shipping the checkout rework tomorrow morning. It moves us from the redirect flow to Checkout Sessions properly — should mean fewer of those timeout retries."}
    {:from :agent :at "2026-07-24T23:19:00Z"
     :text "<p>Noted. One thing from [[Webhook Handling]]: Checkout Sessions arrive as <code>checkout.session.completed</code> with <code>status: \"complete\"</code>, where the invoice path uses <code>\"paid\"</code>. If the handler branches on the literal string, the new flow will not match it.</p><p>Worth a test that asserts both strings provision, before it goes out.</p>"}
